# Wild Honey Pie, opening instrumental break (figure 134.1)
# Seven bars. The essay says all the chords are dominant sevenths, so they are spelled G7, F7 ...
# here (Pollack types the plain letters). The harpsichord's right hand plays descending parallel
# tritones, F/B -> E-flat/A -> D/G# -> C/F#: one to each of the G7, F7, E7 and D7 chords.
# The tritone in the E-flat bar (D-flat/G) is added, following the parallel descent.
#? The essay lists four tritones for five chords; check whether the E-flat bar really has D-flat/G.
#? Octave of the tritones is a guess.
key G

